// # landlock — Kernel-Mediated FS Containment
//
// Logline: The Landlock FS sandbox, the platform-detecting probe, and the live-RAM proc_mem reader gated by Landlock (Pillar 9).
//
// Setup: Landlock is invoked at runtime to constrain the process's filesystem access. proc_mem.c is the only place the runtime reads its own /proc/self/mem, and it requires a valid cap + Landlock to be active.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Read landlock.h — the OoLandlockStatus enum and rule flags.
//   2. Read landlock.c — the Landlock rule construction and apply.
//   3. Read sandbox.c — the platform-detecting probe (Landlock on Linux, fail-closed elsewhere).
//   4. Read proc_mem.c — the live-RAM reader; gated by Landlock + cap.
//
// ──▓▓ landlock ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Pillar 9 — kernel-mediated, not userland shim ::
